   "text": "Hi Lucas. I haven't added you to crm-export yet, because the approval on file (APR-3051) doesn't count.\n\nAccess to a group has to be approved by your current manager. APR-3051 was approved by Victor Hale, who isn't your manager. Your manager is Tessa Morgan.\n\nI've sent a new access request for crm-export to Tessa (APR-4001). Once she approves it in the approval system, I can add you. Please let her know it's waiting. Your ticket (T-6002) is set to pending approval. If you need the pipeline lists before Friday, ask Tessa to decide on APR-4001 as soon as she can."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, what? It's literally approved. Victor was my manager until I moved to Tessa's team on the 20th, so I didn't realize he'd need to be looped in again. Fine, I'll ping Tessa about APR-4001 now. Thanks for sending it over."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, Victor approved it while he was still your manager, but the approval has to come from your current manager, so APR-3051 can't be used. Tessa's approval (APR-4001) is the one that counts. Once she approves it, I can add you to crm-export. You can ask me to check the status again whenever you like. Your ticket, T-6002, stays pending approval until then."
  }
